cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MatchingEngine: Domain-Agnostic Compatibility Scoring with Bounded LLM Adjustment"
authors:
  - given-names: Ni Ni
    family-names: Tin Win
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4794-7391"
abstract: >-
  MatchingEngine is a compatibility-matching system whose scoring core is
  independent of any single industry: the core knows only entities, attributes,
  constraints and weights, while per-domain configuration files supply the
  vocabulary and weights for a given domain. Two domains are implemented against
  the same core — roommate matching and patient-to-therapist matching — and
  adding the second required implementing two scoring roles the core's own design
  had already declared but never built, leaving the first domain's scores
  byte-identical. Matching runs as a three-tier pipeline in which hard filters
  remove non-viable pairs before any scoring, deterministic scoring produces a
  0-90 base from structured attributes, and a bounded large-language-model layer
  reads free-text profiles to adjust that score by at most 10 points in either
  direction, hard-capped in code and degrading to the deterministic result
  whenever a model call fails. The scoring logic is validated by an eval harness
  that combines deterministic unit cases with LLM-based checks for bounds,
  direction, groundedness and run-to-run consistency.
keywords:
  - compatibility matching
  - recommender systems
  - large language models
  - LLM evaluation
  - hybrid scoring
  - constraint-based filtering
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ninitwin4/matching-engine"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-08
